+  <desc id="desc">game.exe calls d3d9.dll through the D3D9 COM API. d3d9.dll holds the COM API and application state, records each frame into fixed records, links mtld3d-core, and calls mtld3d.dll through its exported function mtld3d_unix_call, an ordinary function call. mtld3d.dll crosses the Wine PE/Unix boundary into mtld3d.so, the native runtime, which also links mtld3d-core. Inside mtld3d.so an encoder thread translates the recorded frame into Metal commands, a submit thread replays and commits them, a presenter thread acquires the drawable and presents, and worker threads compile shaders and pipelines and prewarm the shader cache; mtld3d.so drives the Metal framework. The PE side is i386 or x86_64, one chain per architecture, and on an arm64 Wine an x64 game loads ARM64X builds of d3d9.dll and mtld3d.dll instead; the host side is Mach-O in Wine's own architecture.</desc>
